@startuml Simple Contract Management Sequence

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false

title Simple Contract Management - Workflow Sequence

participant "Service Provider\n(SP)" as SP
participant "Compute Provider\n(CP)" as CP
participant "Contract Host\n(Solution Enabler)" as ContractHost
participant "Contract Database" as ContractDB
participant "Contract Actors with\nexecution engine" as ContractActors
participant "SP Computer" as SPComputer
participant "CP Computer" as CPComputer

== Contract Establishment Phase ==

note over SP, CP
  Offline negotiation and agreement
end note

SP <-> CP : 1. Offline agreement and terms formulation of the contract

SP -> ContractHost : 2. Signs Contract via contract package
activate ContractHost

CP -> ContractHost : 3. Signs Contract via contract package

ContractHost -> ContractDB : 4. Store signed contract
activate ContractDB

ContractHost -> ContractActors : 5. Initialize contract actors
activate ContractActors

deactivate ContractHost

== Deployment Request Phase ==

SPComputer -> CPComputer : 6. Request deployment (from SP organization)
activate CPComputer

CPComputer -> ContractActors : 7. Check if valid signed contract exists
ContractActors -> CPComputer : 8. Contract validation result

alt Contract exists and is valid
    CPComputer -> SPComputer : 9a. Accept deployment - deploy and execute
    activate SPComputer
    
    SPComputer -> CPComputer : 10. Job completion notification
    deactivate SPComputer
    
else Contract invalid/unsigned or does not exist
    CPComputer -> SPComputer : 9b. Reject deployment request
end

deactivate CPComputer
deactivate ContractActors
deactivate ContractDB

@enduml